Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Thu Apr 2 22:06:58 2026 +0000
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Thu Apr 2 22:06:58 2026 +0000

    Bug 1902843 - Add compose_scripts and message_display_scripts manifest keys. r=mkmelin

    Adds support for manifest keys to register composeScripts (`compose_scripts`)
    and messageDisplayScripts (`message_display_scripts`), matching the pattern
    used by contentScripts, but without URL matching (the target context is
    obviously fixed).

    - compose_scripts supports js and css properties
    - message_display_scripts supports js, css and run_at properties

    The compose_scripts manifest key, as well as the corresponding API do not
    support `run_at`.

    Implementation details:
    - Add ComposeScript and MessageDisplayScript types.
    - Add onManifestEntry handler in ext-extensionScripts.js that creates
      ExtensionScriptParent instances from manifest entries, reusing the
      existing injection infrastructure.
    - Refactor ExtensionScriptParent to accept either a ProxyContextParent
      (for dynamic register() calls) or an Extension object (for manifest
      entries)

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D290762

